Overtime — Project Requirements Document (PRD)
Version: 3.3 · Engine: GameMaker Studio 2 (GML) · Platform: PC (Windows) first, Steam Deck verification target · Status: In development — M0 vertical slice complete
This document describes the current design only. All decision history — change entries C1–C109, the review and owner-directive coverage maps — lives in CHANGELOG_Overtime.md. Readers never apply deltas: what is written here is what is built. Open items are collected in §18 (R21 tracks the unset floor-hitbox constants that the traversal bands depend on).

1. Executive Summary & Game Overview
1.1 Premise
In a desolate, desert-covered future, humanity's remnants are abruptly abducted by an aggressive cyborg alien race. The player controls a lone human survivor traversing three hostile frontiers — their barren home desert, the sprawling alien carrier vessel, and the alien homeworld — on a high-stakes mission to rescue their species.
1.2 Core gameplay loop & pillars
Genre: 2D side-scrolling action platformer, single player, 30 fps.
Pillar
Concrete systems that deliver it
High-mobility traversal
Precise custom physics (§4.1), dodge-launched sprint and gravity-suspended air dodge with after-images (§5.5), Phase Slash (§5.3)
Tactical resource management
The dual economy — stamina for sprint/dodge/guard, energy for Time Freeze (full-meter gate) and Phase Slash (§5.6) — plus grenade carry limit
Twitch-reflex combat
Mandatory telegraph windows of at least 0.4 s (§6.6), poise and stagger (§6.4), perfect parry (§5.4), unblockable heavy attacks that must be dodged (§6.2, §7.2), frame-perfect hitboxes (§11.3)
Environmental puzzle-solving
Grenade chain detonations (§6.7), Time Freeze repositioning (§5.2)

Structure: three acts, each consisting of 4 generated levels plus 1 hand-built boss arena (15 levels total, §8.1), with a hidden Afterlife state machine (§9) running across the entire campaign.
1.3 The hook
Death does not end the input. At 0 HP the player gets 30 seconds of Overtime to clutch the segment; and if the player keeps dying, the Grim Reaper starts taking it personally.

