5.2 Time Freeze [PLANNED]
Design rules:
Cost: requires the energy meter at exactly full (100); activation drains it to 0 (§5.6). Below full, activation is rejected with a fizzle and an icon flash. Spending Phase Slashes visibly delays the next Freeze — that tension is the point of the shared meter.
Duration 5 s; cooldown 30 s starting at activation (the cooldown usually dominates refuel time; the full-meter gate binds when Phase Slash spending interrupts banking). One charge, no stacking.
Frozen enemies still take damage — at half. Every player damage source (sword, heavy weapons, Phase Slash, grenade blasts) is multiplied by frozen_damage_mult = 0.5 against a frozen enemy or boss part; fractions are kept. A frozen enemy does not flinch: no poise damage is dealt, and no stagger, stun (including the mace shockwave), or knockback applies while it is frozen, because a frozen entity does not change state. A frozen enemy reduced to 0 HP is killed at once by the hit pipeline — kill credit, +5 s of Overtime, +15 energy, drops, and death FX all resolve immediately and the instance is destroyed even though it is not ticking. Frozen hostile projectiles and hazards are not damageable; player attacks pass through them.
Frozen hostiles cannot hurt the player: all hostile hitboxes are disabled while frozen, so contact with a frozen enemy or stopped projectile deals no damage. Time Freeze remains first a defensive and repositioning tool; chipping enemies at half damage with no stagger is a deliberate, limited bonus.
Grenades vs frozen targets: the player is operational during a freeze, so a grenade thrown during one flies normally, is not frozen, and detonates on schedule. Its blast deals half damage to frozen enemies (the same 0.5 multiplier) and still deals full damage to the player (friendly fire). A grenade already in flight when a freeze starts is player-owned and keeps flying under the same rule.
Boss freeze budget: in any boss attempt, the first two activations each last 2.5 s (halved); further activations are rejected until the attempt resets. Bosses and their parts are frozen like any enemy, so they take half damage during a freeze. This stops per-pattern freezing while keeping the repositioning utility.
Fully frozen: regular enemies, boss parts, hostile projectiles, hazards, gameplay particles, gameplay sequences.
Keeps running: ambient background, parallax, HUD, dialogue.
During Overtime State: usable; the Overtime timer is unaffected (§5.1).
Engineering architecture: §11.2 (time domains + the unskippable gate).
