6. Combat System [PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED — refactor to the shared pipeline in M1a]
6.1 Hit pipeline
All damage flows through one hitbox component. Attackers spawn obj_hitbox with a config struct; nothing applies damage per-object anymore.
Frame-bound hitboxes. Every animated attack is frame-perfect: hitbox rectangles live in per-frame hitbox data keyed by (sprite, sprite frame), and the hitbox is live exactly while its owner's sprite frame is inside the bound range (§11.3). Non-animated hazards (beams, shockwave rings, grenade blasts) use a plain lifetime in logic frames instead.
// Animated attack: geometry and lifetime come from the sprite-frame data
scr_hitbox_bound(owner, {
    damage:         18,
    type:           DMG.MELEE,
    team:           TEAM.PLAYER,
    kb_x:           220, kb_y: 0,
    pierces_shield: false,
    bind:           HB.SWORD_ACTIVE     // (sprite, frames a..b) from hitbox data
});


// Non-animated hazard: free geometry and an explicit lifetime
scr_hitbox(x, y, w, h, {
    damage:   30,
    type:     DMG.EXPLOSIVE,
    team:     TEAM.ENEMY,
    lifetime: 6
});
Fields: damage, type (enum DMG), team (enum TEAM: PLAYER / ENEMY / BOSS / NEUTRAL), kb_x / kb_y, pierces_shield, bind or lifetime, optional on_hit callback, optional effect (the STUN type applies a stun instead of damage). The hitbox resolves target eligibility from the friendly-fire matrix (§6.3) and shield rules (§6.2). A frozen target (§5.2) takes the incoming damage multiplied by frozen_damage_mult (0.5) and receives no poise damage, stun, or knockback.
