Behavioral notes:
Standard Cyborg: closes distance directly; the tutorial enemy for telegraph-then-punish. Its heavy overhead is the dodge tutorial (§8.1, L3).
Heavy attacks are uninterruptible. From the first telegraph frame of an enemy heavy attack through its recovery, poise damage still accrues but a poise break is deferred until recovery ends; stun effects (including the mace shockwave) do nothing and do not start the stun-immunity timer; the attacker takes damage normally. Time Freeze suspends the attack and resumes it.
Heavy-attack trigger (anti-turtle): melee variants use their heavy attack when the player has blocked (non-parry) their last 2 attacks, or after the player stays in melee range for 3 s — holding guard is answered, not ignored. Parries do not increment the trigger: a parry already stuns the attacker 2.0 s and resets its aggression timer; counting parries would punish exactly the skill the system exists to reward (§5.4).
Ranger: fires linear ion bolts; backpedals when the player closes inside 240 px. Placement obeys the melee-reachability rule (§7.1).
Grenadier: lobs physics grenades; its friendly fire is a player exploit vector (bait throws into other enemies). Same placement rule.
