Door-mask contract. The mask is the connection contract between adjacent chunks. L/R doors are externalized as continuous floor across the seam; an unconnected edge renders as a cliff (fall = pit death per §4.4). U/D doors connect the surface and underground bands. Phase Slash cannot cross solid terrain (§5.3), so seams and arena bounds need no special barrier objects.
Traversal envelope — derived, then enforced. The generator obeys the physics envelope (§4.1) with coyote time and the floor bonus counted as designed forgiveness, and with a 16 px safety margin on both sides of every band. The bands below are a derivation snapshot at the baseline constants; the validator does not read this table — it simulates the real jump arcs from tuning.json (floor hitbox, coyote, dodge insertion, Phase Slash chain) and asserts tags against the simulation, so a physics tweak re-derives the envelope instead of silently invalidating it (Appendix B).
Tag semantics. A tag names the tools a gap requires, and the validator checks it in both directions:
Tag
Meaning
needs_boost
Crossable by walk-jump + air dodge or by sprint-jump alone; not crossable by a walk-jump
needs_sprint_dodge
Requires sprint-jump and air dodge together; walk + dodge and sprint alone both fall short
needs_phase
Requires a Phase Slash on top of jump + air dodge; sprint + dodge falls short

Band rule. For a tag with allowed chains A and disallowed chains D, a gap of n tiles is legal when 32n > max reach(D) + b + 16 and 32n ≤ min reach(A) + b − 16, where b = floor_w − 2 × floor_overlap.
