Resource-safety rules for gated gaps. A resource-starved or mistimed attempt must never become a pit death — pit deaths bypass Overtime and feed the Reaper counter (§5.1):
Rule
Specification
Recovery platform
Every gated gap's pit (needs_boost, needs_sprint_dodge, needs_phase) contains a 2-tile recovery platform placed on the failure fall arc, plus a stepped climb-back route (walk/climb only, no gated moves) to the takeoff ledge. A failed attempt is a climb back and a retry, never a death. Pits of 15 tiles or more and authored hazards remain lethal
Energy spacing
Consecutive needs_phase gaps are separated by >= 2 full chunks (1280 px, about 5.3 s at walk speed) of gap-free main path — more than the 4.0 s re-bank of one Phase Slash (40 energy at 10/s), so the player always arrives at the next gate able to pay for it
Stamina fairness
needs_boost gaps assume 20 stamina (dodge) or 15 (sprint). needs_sprint_dodge gaps assume a dodge-launched sprint start plus an air dodge: 40 stamina plus the run-up drain in the worst case. The recovery platform catches the empty-tank case

Camera rules. Horizontal lookahead 192 px, eased toward movement direction / facing (lerp 0.10 per frame). Justification: the widest legal gap (14 tiles, 448 px) plus 64 px of landing platform needs 512 px of view ahead of the player; the 320 px half-view plus 192 px of lookahead provides exactly that, so the landing of the longest legal traversal is always on screen (the view behind the player shrinks to 128 px, which is enough because the level scrolls rightward). Vertical: the camera centers on the player with a small 48 px look-down bias while falling fast; boss arenas override with a static lock (§10.5).
The validator. A validator script asserts the full envelope over 100 seeded generations — not by re-reading the band table, but by simulating each main-path gap with the live tuning.json physics: floor hitbox, coyote window, technique chains (the chain enumeration and pseudocode are Appendix B). It additionally asserts: recovery platforms exist and their climb-back routes flood-fill to the takeoff ledge using only walk/climb moves; energy spacing between needs_phase gaps; the melee-reachability placement rule for Rangers and Grenadiers (§7.1); climb caps and U/D platform stacks; door-mask welding; marker sanity; and that no gap lands on a dead tile. It is part of AC21 and runs in the M1c exit gate.
