Generator behavior. Strong rightward bias on the main path; up to 2 probabilistic underground dips per level (mesa/rock fill forms the surface bulge above a dip); single-tile treasure spurs off the main path.
Determinism & RNG isolation. GML exposes one global RNG stream, so the game does not use random() in generator or spawner code at all. Two struct-based PRNGs (mulberry32) are created at boot:
gen_rng = scr_prng_new(level_seed);  // chunk selection, dips, spurs — deterministic per level
fx_rng  = scr_prng_new(run_seed);    // drops, spew intervals, cosmetic variance
