11. Engineering Standards (GameMaker Studio 2)
11.1 Movement & collision, timestep [IMPLEMENTED — 30 fps port in M1a]
Custom velocity mandate: hsp/vsp + manual collision sweeps; built-in vspeed, gravity, friction banned in gameplay objects. Fixed 30 fps logic (room speed 30) — the M1a port changes room speed and re-derives every frame-count constant (§4.1, §19). The replay harness runs before and after the port; because the port changes the integration step, step 2 re-baselines the state hash and the pre/post comparison uses tolerance traces (position and time within bounds), not hash equality (§15.2). The dodge writes hsp = 480 * dir for its 6 f duration; a ground dodge leaves gravity on the first unsupported frame, while an air dodge cancels all vertical momentum — vsp is set to 0, gravity is suspended for those 6 f, and the fall resumes from vsp = 0 with nothing restored (§5.5).
