11.2 Time domains & the Time Freeze architecture [PLANNED — design locked]
GameMaker has no native per-object time scale, and an "everyone remembers to check the flag" Step bypass fails silently for new objects, does not stop alarms, and leaves Begin/End Step and Collision events running. The architecture is structural, not conventional:
One time-domain manager. Pause, dialogue pause, hitstop (2 f at 30 fps), and freeze are four separate mechanisms in most GameMaker projects and clobber each other (hitstop ending mid-freeze, dialogue racing a stun). Here a single manager arbitrates:
