Appendix B — Reachability Validator (simulation spec)
The traversal bands in §8.4 are a derivation snapshot. The validator never reads them — it re-derives the envelope from tuning.json by simulation, so a physics tweak cannot silently invalidate AC21. This appendix is the specification for that validator.
B.1 Inputs
Everything the simulation uses comes from global.cfg (loaded from tuning.json, §11.6) — the same file that drives the game:
floor_w, floor_overlap    floor hitbox width and minimum support overlap (px)   [24, 1 — R21]
walk, sprint, dodge_speed horizontal speeds (px/s)
dodge_time                dodge duration (s) — gravity suspended inside (air dodge only)
jump_v                    jump velocity (px/s, negative)
g_rise, g_fall            gravity constants (px/s²)
vsp_max                   terminal fall speed (px/s)
jump_cut_v                variable-jump cut clamp (px/s)
coyote                    coyote window (s) — carried horizontal speed after a walking/sprinting ledge exit
air_accel                 air acceleration toward the latched takeoff speed (px/s²)   [1200]
takeoff_clamp             jump takeoff hsp clamp (px/s)      [330]
dodge_exit_clamp          dodge exit hsp clamp (px/s)        [330]
phase_distance            Phase Slash teleport (px)          [160]
margin                    band safety margin per side (px)   [16]
TILE                      32
B.2 Simulated primitives
Each primitive replays a real arc against a flat gap at equal takeoff/landing height, using the true floor hitbox and tile collision — not closed-form math:
Floor geometry. Takeoff: the origin may stand up to floor_w/2 − floor_overlap past the ledge edge. Landing: the leading edge must reach gap + floor_overlap. The net floor bonus is b = floor_w − 2 × floor_overlap.
sim_jump(speed) — full-hold jump arc at speed: rise under g_rise, fall under g_fall to return to takeoff height; horizontal distance = speed x airtime.
sim_coyote(speed) — the same arc launched coyote seconds after leaving a ledge by walking or sprinting (horizontal speed carried at full value during the window).
sim_air_dodge(arc) — inserts the dodge at the best legal logic frame of the arc (the search tries every frame; one dodge per airtime, subject to the end-anchored cooldown). The dodge cancels all vertical momentum: vsp is set to 0 and gravity is suspended for dodge_time while horizontal runs at dodge_speed; afterwards hsp = min(dodge_speed, dodge_exit_clamp) returns to the latched takeoff speed at air_accel, and the fall resumes from vsp = 0 (nothing is restored). A dodge during the rise ends the rise (a loss of reach); a dodge during the fall resets the fall speed (a gain of airtime). The best timing at the baseline constants is about 0.22 s after the apex. Air speed model: hsp in the air is latched to the takeoff speed class (walk 240 or sprint 330).
sim_phase(chain) — appends phase_distance at the chain's end position (hsp preserved); the slash stops at the first solid, so it never crosses a wall.
sim_ledge_dodge() — a ground dodge that leaves the ground: dash for the remainder of the burst, gravity on from the first unsupported frame, no coyote, jump input buffered until landing, air dodge available only after the end-anchored cooldown.
sim_dodge_jump() — ground dodge held into a jump: takeoff hsp clamped to takeoff_clamp, so the result equals the sprint-jump chain by construction (the simulation verifies the clamp rather than trusting it).
