Band rule. A gap of n tiles is legal for a tag when 32n > max effective(D) + margin and 32n <= min effective(A) − margin. Applying it to the table above:
needs_boost: 32n > 205 + 16 = 221 and 32n <= 274 − 16 = 258, so n = 7-8.
needs_sprint_dodge: 32n > 336 + 16 = 352 and 32n <= 413 − 16 = 397, so n = 11-12.
needs_phase: 32n > 413 + 16 = 429 and 32n <= 496 − 16 = 480 (the upper bound, 479.9 px at unrounded values, excludes 15 tiles = 480 px), so n = 14.
Dead tiles are the widths between 5 and 14 that fall in no band: 5, 6, 9, 10, 13. Gaps of 15 or more are forbidden. The authored untagged main-path limit is 4 tiles (CH0 would cross 5 with margin).
Assertions (per generation, 100 seeds):
For every main-path gap: width <= 4 x TILE when untagged; when tagged, the tag's band rule holds against the live simulation (tag honesty in both directions — the weakest allowed chain crosses it, the strongest disallowed chain does not).
Tag/level gating: needs_sprint_dodge only at L2+; needs_phase only at L6+.
No gap lands on a dead tile; no gap >= 15 x TILE anywhere on the main path.
Every gated gap's pit contains a 2-tile recovery platform on the failure fall arc; a flood fill from the platform to the takeoff ledge using walk/climb moves only must succeed.
Consecutive needs_phase gaps are >= 2 chunks apart on the main path.
Every Ranger/Grenadier marker's platform passes the melee-reachability check: connected to a mandatory-path platform through CH0 terrain only (no gated gap).
CH6 negative assertion: a ledge-dodge chain never crosses a gap CH0 cannot, and no chain that starts with a dodge-initiated ledge exit exceeds CH0's effective reach.
Climb <= 3 tiles per seam; U/D chunks contain platform stacks.
Door masks weld across all seams; every spur is bidirectionally reachable.
Marker sanity: no enemy spawn inside solid, no marker beyond chunk bounds.
Output: per-seed pass/fail with the offending gap, its simulated crossing table (which chains clear it), and the tuning constants used — a physics-tweak regression report, not just a red/green flag. A change to any physics or floor-hitbox constant regenerates the band table and flags every tagged slot whose tag no longer holds.
B.5 Implementation notes
The simulator reuses the game's own collision routines (scr_move_h_collide / scr_move_v_collide) against a scratch tilemap of the generated chunk chain — the same code the player runs, so "the validator says it's crossable" and "the player can cross it" are the same statement.
Determinism: the validator runs on the gen_rng stream after generation, consuming no gameplay-relevant RNG draws.
It runs in CI on every tuning.json change (AC21 in the M1c exit gate), and its per-gap crossing table is written next to templates.json for level designers.
